pub fn next_record(&mut self) -> Option<Record<'a>> {
    if self.stopped { return None; }
    loop {
        if self.header().is_err() { return None; }
        if self.pos >= self.buf.len() {
            self.stopped = true;
            return None;   // status remains Clean if it was Clean
        }
        let expected = self.last_seq.map(|s| s.wrapping_add(1)); // Option<u64>
        match parse_record_at(self.buf, self.pos, expected) {
            Ok(rec) => {
                self.last_seq = Some(rec.header.seq);
                self.consumed = self.pos + rec.header.record_len();
                self.pos = self.consumed;
                self.records += 1;
                return Some(rec);
            }
            Err(_) => {
                // resync
                match self.resync() {
                    Some(next) => { self.pos = next; /* loop continues: will parse and yield */ }
                    None => { self.stopped = true; return None; }
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
```
Careful: `expected` in primary path: if last_seq is None (first record) then expected = Some(header.seq_first)? Better: expected = if last_seq None → Some(self.header.seq_first) since header declares seq_first. Hmm, but "seq strictly sequential" — reader could require first record seq == header.seq_first. Does that help? It would reject a segment whose first record was corrupt... but then resync branch handles recovery. For the truncation test with t ≥ 64: first record seq = seq_first ✓. Let me implement: expected = Some(self.last_seq.map_or(header.seq_first, |s| s + 1)). But if header.seq_first mismatches actual first seq (shouldn't happen) → resync → damaged. Fine.

Hmm, careful: resync requires seq > last_seq when last_seq is Some; when None, allow seq >= seq_first. Implement helper.

resync:
```rust
/// Сканирует байт за байтом от pos+1 в поисках следующей валидной записи.
/// Возвращает смещение записи; при неудаче фиксирует статус Torn/Damaged и None.
fn resync(&mut self) -> Option<usize> {
    let start = self.pos;
    let min_seq = match self.last_seq { Some(s) => s + 1, None => self.header.map_or(0, |h| h.seq_first) };
    let mut candidate = start + 1;
    while candidate + RECORD_HEADER_LEN <= self.buf.len() {
        if self.buf[candidate..candidate+4] == RECORD_MAGIC_BYTES {
            if let Ok(rec) = parse_record_at(self.buf, candidate, None) {
                if rec.header.seq >= min_seq {
                    // потерянные записи: файл повреждён, но хвост читаем
                    if self.status == ReaderStatus::Clean { self.status = ReaderStatus::Damaged { at: start }; }
                    return Some(candidate);
                }
            }
        }
        candidate += 1;
    }
    // дальше валидных записей нет: различаем обрыв и повреждение
    let magic_present = start + 4 <= self.buf.len() && self.buf[start..start+4] == RECORD_MAGIC_BYTES;
    self.status = if magic_present { ReaderStatus::Torn { at: start } } else { ReaderStatus::Damaged { at: start } };
    None
}
