```rust
fn parse_at(&self, offset: usize, expected: Option<u64>) -> Result<Record<'a>, Error>
```
with explicit 'a — but `&self` borrow; returning Record<'a> from self.buf is fine since 'a outlives the &self borrow? The signature says returns Record<'a>; inside `parse_record_at(self.buf, offset)?` gives Record<'a> ✓.

`next_record(&mut self) -> Option<Record<'a>>` ✓.

